    "project_template_level_name": "csp-unit2-lesson24-template_27_28",
    "teacher_markdown": "- Students keep the loop line `for j in range(count):` as it is. Validate looks for exactly that line.\r\n- Students write six lines: `total = 0`, the `input()` line with `int()`, the total update, `average`, and two prints. Check that these are theirs, not AI Tutor's.\r\n- Validate checks the algorithm only: that each pass uses the typed number, that `total` is the running total, that `average` is the total divided by `count`, and that the total and then the average are printed. It runs without Theater, so it does not check the picture.\r\n- If AI Tutor's pasted code changes `value` or `total`, Validate fails and says so.\r\n- If the program crashes when students run it, the error is usually in the pasted drawing code. Common causes are a color name outside the Theater palette, a negative width or height, a note outside 48 to 84, or too many pauses, since an animation is limited to 600 frames.\r\n- Common mistakes: forgetting `int()`, starting `total` inside the loop, so it resets, dividing by `j` instead of `count`, and computing `average` before the loop finishes.\r\n- Expected result for the numbers 40, 55, 30, 60, 25, 45, 35: total 290, average about 41.43.\r\n- Students will see `story_review.txt` in their files. It is for the next level, so ask students to leave it for now.\r\n- Challenge: Validate still passes if students print an extra line after the total and average.\r\n- If a student uses Build Python, they still own the sum and average. Ask them to point to the line that adds each number to the total.\r\n- Use this level to check whether students can write a running total and an average in a loop, and decide what to keep, change, or reject from AI-generated code.",
    "validation_file": {
      "id": "3",
      "name": "test.py",
      "contents": "import ast\nimport io\nimport re\nimport sys\nimport types\nfrom contextlib import redirect_stdout\nfrom unittest import TestCase\n\n# Three sets of typed numbers, so a program that ignores input() cannot pass.\nFAKE_RUNS = [\n    [40, 55, 30, 60, 25, 45, 35, 50, 20, 65, 15, 70, 10, 75],\n    [20, 60, 20, 60, 20, 60, 20, 60, 20, 60, 20, 60, 20, 60],\n    [10, 10, 10, 10, 10, 10, 10, 10, 10, 10, 10, 10, 10, 10],\n]\nMISSING = 'MISSING'\nTHEATER_NAMES = [\n    'clear', 'remove_stroke_color', 'remove_fill_color', 'set_fill_color', 'set_stroke_color',\n    'set_stroke_width', 'draw_rectangle', 'draw_ellipse', 'draw_line', 'draw_text', 'draw_shape',\n    'draw_regular_polygon', 'draw_image', 'set_text_color', 'set_text_height', 'set_text_style',\n    'pause', 'play', 'play_note', 'play_note_and_pause', 'play_sound',\n]\n# Theater's fixed palette. Any other color name stops the program.\nPALETTE = {'white', 'silver', 'gray', 'black', 'red', 'maroon', 'yellow', 'olive', 'lime', 'green', 'aqua',\n           'teal', 'blue', 'navy', 'fuchsia', 'purple', 'pink', 'orange', 'gold', 'brown', 'chocolate', 'tan',\n           'turquoise', 'indigo', 'violet', 'beige', 'ivory'}\n\n\nclass FakeColor:\n    def __init__(self, *args):\n        if len(args) != 3 or not all(isinstance(a, (int, float)) and not isinstance(a, bool) for a in args):\n            raise ValueError(\"Color needs three channel values\")\n\n\ndef check_color(color):\n    \"\"\"The same rule as Theater: a palette name, a hex string like #rgb or #rrggbb, or a Color.\"\"\"\n    if isinstance(color, FakeColor):\n        return\n    if isinstance(color, str) and (color.lower() in PALETTE or re.fullmatch(r'#(?:[0-9a-fA-F]{3}|[0-9a-fA-F]{6})', color)):\n        return\n    raise ValueError(f\"Invalid color {color!r}\")\n\n\ndef check_numbers(*values):\n    if any(not isinstance(v, (int, float)) or isinstance(v, bool) for v in values):\n        raise TypeError(\"Positions, sizes, and durations must be numbers\")\n\n\ndef make_stub_theater():\n    \"\"\"A quiet stand-in for theater. It draws nothing, but it raises the errors Theater would raise at the call.\"\"\"\n    stub = types.ModuleType('theater')\n    for name in THEATER_NAMES:\n        setattr(stub, name, lambda *args, **kwargs: None)\n    for name in ('clear', 'set_fill_color', 'set_stroke_color', 'set_text_color'):\n        setattr(stub, name, lambda color: check_color(color))\n\n    def draw_rectangle(x, y, width, height):\n        check_numbers(x, y, width, height)\n        if width < 0 or height < 0:\n            raise ValueError(\"Width and height cannot be negative\")\n\n    def draw_text(text, x, y, rotation=0):\n        if not isinstance(text, str):\n            raise TypeError(\"draw_text needs a string\")\n        check_numbers(x, y)\n\n    def set_text_height(height):\n        check_numbers(height)\n        if not 1 <= height <= 1600:\n            raise ValueError(\"Text height must be between 1 and 1600\")\n\n    def pause(seconds):\n        check_numbers(seconds)\n        if not 0.1 <= seconds <= 655.35:\n            raise ValueError(\"A pause must be between 0.1 and 655.35 seconds\")\n\n    def play_note(note, duration):\n        check_numbers(note, duration)\n        if not 48 <= note <= 84:\n            raise ValueError(\"A note must be between 48 and 84\")\n        if not 0.1 <= duration <= 655.35:\n            raise ValueError(\"A note duration must be between 0.1 and 655.35 seconds\")\n\n    def play_note_and_pause(note, duration):\n        play_note(note, duration)\n\n    stub.draw_rectangle = stub.draw_ellipse = draw_rectangle\n    stub.draw_text = draw_text\n    stub.set_text_height = set_text_height\n    stub.pause = pause\n    stub.play_note = play_note\n    stub.play_note_and_pause = play_note_and_pause\n    stub.get_width = lambda *args, **kwargs: 400\n    stub.get_height = lambda *args, **kwargs: 400\n    stub.Color = FakeColor\n    stub.__all__ = THEATER_NAMES + ['get_width', 'get_height', 'Color']\n    return stub\n\n\nclass AddSnapshot(ast.NodeTransformer):\n    \"\"\"Adds a snapshot call at the end of the main loop, which must be: for j in range(count).\"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(self):\n        self.found = False\n\n    def visit_Module(self, node):\n        for statement in node.body:\n            if (isinstance(statement, ast.For) and isinstance(statement.iter, ast.Call)\n                    and isinstance(statement.iter.func, ast.Name) and statement.iter.func.id == 'range'\n                    and len(statement.iter.args) == 1 and isinstance(statement.iter.args[0], ast.Name)\n                    and statement.iter.args[0].id == 'count'):\n                call = ast.Call(func=ast.Name(id='__snapshot__', ctx=ast.Load()), args=[], keywords=[])\n                statement.body.append(ast.Expr(value=call))\n                self.found = True\n        return node\n\n\ndef run_program(fed):\n    \"\"\"Run main.py once with the typed numbers in fed. Record value and total after every pass of the main loop.\"\"\"\n    with open('main.py') as main_file:\n        source = main_file.read()\n    output = io.StringIO()\n    snapshots = []\n    error = None\n    found = False\n    typed = iter(fed)\n    fake_globals = {'__name__': '__main__', 'input': lambda prompt='': str(next(typed))}\n    fake_globals['__snapshot__'] = lambda: snapshots.append({\n        'value': fake_globals.get('value', MISSING), 'total': fake_globals.get('total', MISSING)})\n    real_theater = sys.modules.get('theater')\n    sys.modules['theater'] = make_stub_theater()\n    try:\n        transformer = AddSnapshot()\n        tree = transformer.visit(ast.parse(source))\n        found = transformer.found\n        ast.fix_missing_locations(tree)\n        with redirect_stdout(output):\n            exec(compile(tree, 'main.py', 'exec'), fake_globals)\n    except Exception as e:\n        error = e\n    finally:\n        if real_theater is None:\n            sys.modules.pop('theater', None)\n        else:\n            sys.modules['theater'] = real_theater\n    lines = [line for line in output.getvalue().splitlines() if line.strip()]\n    final = {key: fake_globals.get(key, MISSING) for key in ('count', 'total', 'average', 'splits_evenly')}\n    return lines, snapshots, final, found, error\n\n\ndef settings_ok(final):\n    return isinstance(final['count'], int) and not isinstance(final['count'], bool) and 1 <= final['count'] <= 14\n\n\ndef prepare(test, fed):\n    \"\"\"Run the program and make sure the main loop ran count times.\"\"\"\n    lines, snapshots, final, found, error = run_program(fed)\n    if error:\n        test.skipTest(\"Fix the error first, then we can check this.\")\n    if not found:\n        test.skipTest(\"Keep the loop line as it is: for j in range(count):\")\n    if not settings_ok(final):\n        test.skipTest(\"Keep count as a whole number from 1 to 14.\")\n    if len(snapshots) != final['count']:\n        test.skipTest(\"We didn't find your loop running count times, so we can't check this yet.\")\n    return lines, snapshots, final\n\n\nclass TestSumAverage(TestCase):\n    def test_1_runs_without_error(self):\n        \"\"\"Your program runs without an error\"\"\"\n        for number, fed in enumerate(FAKE_RUNS, 1):\n            lines, snapshots, final, found, error = run_program(fed)\n            if error:\n                message = str(error)\n                hint = \"Read the error message, then check the lines you wrote and the code you pasted in.\"\n                if isinstance(error, ZeroDivisionError):\n                    hint = \"Something divided by zero. Check what you divide by.\"\n                elif isinstance(error, StopIteration):\n                    hint = \"Your program asked for more numbers than expected. Keep count at 14 or less.\"\n                elif 'Invalid color' in message:\n                    hint = \"Theater only knows its 27 palette color names, hex colors like #1B1B3A, and Color(red, green, blue).\"\n                elif 'draw_text needs a string' in message:\n                    hint = \"draw_text needs text. Turn a number into text with str() first.\"\n                elif 'negative' in message:\n                    hint = \"A shape was given a negative width or height. Check the numbers that set its size.\"\n                elif 'pause' in message.lower() or 'note' in message.lower() or 'text height' in message.lower():\n                    hint = \"Theater only accepts pauses of 0.1 seconds or more, notes from 48 to 84, and text heights from 1 to 1600.\"\n                elif isinstance(error, TypeError):\n                    hint = \"Two different types were combined. Check that you turned the typed text into a number, and that pasted code gives each command the right kind of value.\"\n                self.fail(f\"Your program stopped with a {type(error).__name__} ({message}) when the numbers were set {number}. {hint}\")\n\n    def test_2_main_loop(self):\n        \"\"\"Your main loop runs once for each number, with the line: for j in range(count):\"\"\"\n        for number, fed in enumerate(FAKE_RUNS, 1):\n            lines, snapshots, final, found, error = run_program(fed)\n            if error:\n                self.skipTest(\"Fix the error first, then we can check this.\")\n            if not found:\n                self.fail(\"We didn't find the line for j in range(count): at the top level. Keep that line as it is.\")\n            if not settings_ok(final):\n                self.fail(\"Keep count as a whole number from 1 to 14.\")\n            if len(snapshots) != final['count']:\n                self.fail(\"Your main loop should run once for each number. Check count and your loop.\")\n\n    def test_3_typed_numbers(self):\n        \"\"\"Each pass uses the number the user types\"\"\"\n        for number, fed in enumerate(FAKE_RUNS, 1):\n            lines, snapshots, final = prepare(self, fed)\n            for index, snap in enumerate(snapshots):\n                if snap['value'] == MISSING:\n                    self.fail(\"We could not find a variable named value. Use the name from the instructions.\")\n                if snap['value'] != fed[index]:\n                    self.fail(f\"On pass {index + 1}, value was {snap['value']} but the number typed in was {fed[index]}. \"\n                              \"Ask for the number with input(), turn it into an int, and make sure pasted drawing code does not change value.\")\n\n    def test_4_running_total(self):\n        \"\"\"total is the running total after every pass\"\"\"\n        for number, fed in enumerate(FAKE_RUNS, 1):\n            lines, snapshots, final = prepare(self, fed)\n            if any(snap['value'] != fed[i] for i, snap in enumerate(snapshots)):\n                self.skipTest(\"Get your input working first, then we can check this.\")\n            running = 0\n            for index, snap in enumerate(snapshots):\n                running += fed[index]\n                if snap['total'] == MISSING:\n                    self.fail(\"We could not find a variable named total. Use the name from the instructions.\")\n                if snap['total'] != running:\n                    self.fail(f\"After pass {index + 1}, total was {snap['total']} but it should be {running}. \"\n                              \"Check where total starts and how you add each number. Pasted drawing code must not change total.\")\n\n    def test_5_average(self):\n        \"\"\"average is the total divided by count, after the loop\"\"\"\n        for number, fed in enumerate(FAKE_RUNS, 1):\n            lines, snapshots, final = prepare(self, fed)\n            if any(snap['value'] != fed[i] for i, snap in enumerate(snapshots)):\n                self.skipTest(\"Get your input working first, then we can check this.\")\n            want_total = sum(fed[:final['count']])\n            if final['total'] != want_total:\n                self.skipTest(\"Fix your total first, then we can check this.\")\n            if final['average'] == MISSING:\n                self.fail(\"We could not find a variable named average. Use the name from the instructions.\")\n            want = want_total / final['count']\n            if not isinstance(final['average'], (int, float)) or abs(final['average'] - want) > 1e-9:\n                self.fail(f\"average was {final['average']} but it should be {want}. \"\n                          \"Check what you divide by, and make sure it comes after the loop.\")\n\n    def test_6_splits_evenly(self):\n        \"\"\"splits_evenly is True when total divides evenly by count, and False if not\"\"\"\n        for number, fed in enumerate(FAKE_RUNS, 1):\n            lines, snapshots, final = prepare(self, fed)\n            if any(snap['value'] != fed[i] for i, snap in enumerate(snapshots)):\n                self.skipTest(\"Get your input working first, then we can check this.\")\n            want_total = sum(fed[:final['count']])\n            if final['total'] != want_total:\n                self.skipTest(\"Fix your total first, then we can check this.\")\n            if final['splits_evenly'] == MISSING:\n                self.fail(\"We could not find a variable named splits_evenly. Use the name from the instructions.\")\n            want = want_total % final['count'] == 0\n            if not isinstance(final['splits_evenly'], bool) or final['splits_evenly'] != want:\n                self.fail(f\"splits_evenly was {final['splits_evenly']} but it should be {want} when the total is {want_total} and count is {final['count']}. \"\n                          \"Use % to find the remainder, and compare it to 0 so you get True or False.\")\n\n    def test_7_prints(self):\n        \"\"\"You print the total, then the average, then splits_evenly\"\"\"\n        for number, fed in enumerate(FAKE_RUNS, 1):\n            lines, snapshots, final = prepare(self, fed)\n            want_total = sum(fed[:final['count']])\n            want_average = want_total / final['count']\n            numbers = [[float(n) for n in re.findall(r'-?\\d+(?:\\.\\d+)?', line)] for line in lines]\n            total_line = next((i for i, nums in enumerate(numbers) if any(abs(n - want_total) < 0.01 for n in nums)), None)\n            if total_line is None:\n                self.fail(f\"We didn't find the total ({want_total}) in your printed lines. Print the total.\")\n            average_line = next((i for i, nums in enumerate(numbers)\n                                 if i > total_line and any(abs(n - want_average) < 0.01 for n in nums)), None)\n            if average_line is None:\n                self.fail(f\"We didn't find the average ({want_average}) printed after the total. Print the total first, then the average.\")\n            want_split = want_total % final['count'] == 0\n            if not any(str(want_split) in line for line in lines[average_line + 1:]):\n                self.fail(f\"We didn't find splits_evenly ({want_split}) printed after the average. Print the total, then the average, then splits_evenly.\")",
      "folderId": "0",
      "active": false,
      "type": "validation"
    }
  },
  "published": true,
  "audit_log": "[{\"changed_at\":\"2026-11-12T05:26:04.084+00:00\",\"changed\":[\"cloned from \\\"csp-unit2-lesson5-make_27_28\\\"\"],\"cloned_from\":\"csp-unit2-lesson5-make_27_28\"},{\"changed_at\":\"2026-11-12 05:26:35 +0000\",\"changed\":[\"long_instructions\",\"predict_settings\",\"ai_tutor_prompt_settings\"],\"changed_by_id\":19378,\"changed_by_email\":\"cody.diliberto@code.org\"},{\"changed_at\":\"2026-11-13 05:02:14 +0000\",\"changed\":[],\"changed_by_id\":19378,\"changed_by_email\":\"cody.diliberto@code.org\"},{\"changed_at\":\"2026-11-13 05:02:38 +0000\",\"changed\":[\"start_sources\"],\"changed_by_id\":19378,\"changed_by_email\":\"cody.diliberto@code.org\"},{\"changed_at\":\"2026-11-13 05:37:05 +0000\",\"changed\":[\"start_sources\"],\"changed_by_id\":19378,\"changed_by_email\":\"cody.diliberto@code.org\"},{\"changed_at\":\"2026-11-13 06:02:26 +0000\",\"changed\":[\"long_instructions\",\"predict_settings\"],\"changed_by_id\":19378,\"changed_by_email\":\"cody.diliberto@code.org\"},{\"changed_at\":\"2026-11-13 06:07:21 +0000\",\"changed\":[\"encrypted_exemplar_sources\"],\"changed_by_id\":19378,\"changed_by_email\":\"cody.diliberto@code.org\"},{\"changed_at\":\"2026-11-13 06:10:12 +0000\",\"changed\":[\"long_instructions\",\"predict_settings\",\"teacher_markdown\"],\"changed_by_id\":19378,\"changed_by_email\":\"cody.diliberto@code.org\"},{\"changed_at\":\"2026-11-13 06:10:31 +0000\",\"changed\":[\"predict_settings\"],\"changed_by_id\":19378,\"changed_by_email\":\"cody.diliberto@code.org\"},{\"changed_at\":\"2026-11-13 06:34:17 +0000\",\"changed\":[\"predict_settings\",\"teacher_markdown\"],\"changed_by_id\":19378,\"changed_by_email\":\"cody.diliberto@code.org\"},{\"changed_at\":\"2026-11-13 07:20:02 +0000\",\"changed\":[\"encrypted_exemplar_sources\"],\"changed_by_id\":19378,\"changed_by_email\":\"cody.diliberto@code.org\"},{\"changed_at\":\"2026-11-13 07:49:38 +0000\",\"changed\":[\"predict_settings\",\"ai_tutor_prompt_settings\"],\"changed_by_id\":19378,\"changed_by_email\":\"cody.diliberto@code.org\"},{\"changed_at\":\"2026-11-13 08:24:01 +0000\",\"changed\":[\"predict_settings\",\"ai_tutor_prompt_settings\"],\"changed_by_id\":19378,\"changed_by_email\":\"cody.diliberto@code.org\"},{\"changed_at\":\"2026-11-13 08:46:54 +0000\",\"changed\":[\"encrypted_exemplar_sources\"],\"changed_by_id\":19378,\"changed_by_email\":\"cody.diliberto@code.org\"},{\"changed_at\":\"2026-11-13 20:07:22 +0000\",\"changed\":[\"start_sources\"],\"changed_by_id\":19378,\"changed_by_email\":\"cody.diliberto@code.org\"},{\"changed_at\":\"2026-11-13 20:08:09 +0000\",\"changed\":[\"start_sources\"],\"changed_by_id\":19378,\"changed_by_email\":\"cody.diliberto@code.org\"}]"
